2697:      "candidate_contract": "| `thm-borel-localization-for-compact-torus-actions` | theorem | For a compact smooth `T`-manifold and rational or real coefficients, define the multiplicative set generated by nonzero characters of `T`. Prove restriction to the fixed locus `M^T` becomes an isomorphism after that localization, with its precise compactness/finite-type hypotheses. The proof needs the fixed-set submanifold, a `T`-invariant tubular neighborhood, the equivariant Thom/Gysin map and the fact that each normal weight is invertible in the localized coefficient ring. On the complement, give a finite orbit-type/slice cover; each proper isotropy subgroup has a nonzero character vanishing on its identity component, so its equivariant cohomology is torsion after localization. State separately any properness/compact-support version for noncompact spaces. |",
