items/lem-nrqm-photons-transverse-fock-total-momentum.md:110:2.1 [Symmetry includes polarization permutations] Define the unitary $\tau_\pi$ on $(\mathbb C^3)^{\otimes n}$ by the same tensor-factor permutation as in [F2]. The conjugated ambient permutation is $(C_\pi u)(k_1,\ldots,k_n)=\tau_\pi u(k_{\widehat{\pi}(1)},\ldots,k_{\widehat{\pi}(n)})$: substitution into the elementary product formula verifies this identity, and the bounded maps agree everywhere by density. Its average $S_n=(n!)^{-1}\sum_\pi C_\pi$ is the orthogonal symmetry projection. The tensor projection $(M_\Pi)^{\otimes n}$ commutes with every ambient permutation, as is verified on elementary tensors, so $M_{Q_n}$ commutes with $S_n$. Their product $R_n=M_{Q_n}S_n$ is an orthogonal projection, whose range is exactly the image of the symmetric transverse tensor sector. Thus $K_n=\operatorname{ran}R_n$ and $I_n=\Theta_n$ restricted to that sector is an isometry onto $K_n$. Every bounded scalar multiplier $b(p_{j,n})$ commutes with $M_{Q_n}$ pointwise and with $C_\pi$, since $p_{j,n}$ is invariant under permutations; therefore it commutes with $R_n$ and preserves $K_n$. [step 1.1, F1, F2, algebra]
