items/pthm-cm09-averaging-for-weak-damping.md:125:[F4] Averaging theorem ([[thm-cm-averaging-for-fast-periodic-oscillations]] and [[def-cm-averaging-data-and-averaged-field]]) with state space $O=\mathbb C\cong\mathbb R^{2}$: for a continuous field $f:\mathbb R\times O\to O$ with continuous partial derivatives in the state, $P$-periodic in $t$, satisfying $\lVert f(t,\zeta)\rVert_{2}\le M$ and $\lVert D_{\zeta}f(t,\zeta)\rVert\le L$ for $\lVert\zeta-\zeta_{0}\rVert_{2}\le R$ ([[def-metric-ball]], [[def-operator-norm]]), and for a solution $\bar\zeta$ of $\bar\zeta'=\varepsilon\bar f(\bar\zeta)$ with $\bar\zeta(0)=\zeta_{0}$ that lies in $\overline B(\zeta_{0},R-\rho)$ on $[0,A/\varepsilon]$, the hypothesis $\varepsilon K<\rho$ with $K=e^{LA}\bigl[B+(LB+B_{1}M)A\bigr]$, $B=2MP$, $B_{1}=2LP$, implies that the solution of $\zeta'=\varepsilon f(t,\zeta)$, $\zeta(0)=\zeta_{0}$ exists on $[0,A/\varepsilon]$ and satisfies $\lVert\zeta(t)-\bar\zeta(t)\rVert_{2}\le\varepsilon K$ there.
