items/lem-gr-finite-smooth-volume-density.md:74:[L1] $M$ is a smooth four-manifold: Hausdorff, second countable, locally Euclidean, and coordinate balls form a basis; consequently there is a countable open cover by relatively compact coordinate charts, and for every such cover there is a smooth partition of unity subordinate to it, locally finite and with values in $[0,1]$ summing to one ([[def-smooth-manifold]], [[lem-coordinate-balls-form-a-basis-of-a-topological-manifold]], [[def-smooth-partition-of-unity-subordinate-to-an-open-cover]], [[cor-smooth-partitions-subordinate-to-a-countable-coordinate-cover]], [[def-countable-choice]]).
items/lem-gr-finite-smooth-volume-density.md:78:[L3] Gluing and measure: a nonnegative density together with a countable locally finite chart cover and a subordinate smooth partition of unity defines a countably additive nonnegative Borel measure $\mu_r$ by the displayed chart formula, independent of the cover and partition; for a positive smooth density $\mu_r$ is finite on compact sets, locally finite and $\sigma$-finite, and regular Borel ([[def-countable-chart-gluing-of-a-nonnegative-density-measure]], [[thm-chart-gluing-defines-a-countably-additive-borel-density-measure]], [[thm-density-measure-is-independent-of-the-chart-gluing]], [[thm-a-positive-smooth-density-defines-a-locally-finite-radon-measure]]).
items/lem-gr-finite-smooth-volume-density.md:90:1.1 (A countable cover adapted to the metric.) By [L1] choose a countable cover $\{U_i\}_{i\ge1}$ of $M$ by relatively compact coordinate charts $(U_i,x_i)$ and a smooth partition of unity $\{\rho_i\}$ subordinate to it, so that $\rho_i$ has compact support in $U_i$, only finitely many $\rho_i$ are nonzero near any point, and $\sum_i\rho_i=1$. For each $i$ let $\delta_i$ be the density supported in $U_i$ whose coefficient in the chart $x_i$ is $\rho_i\cdot w$, where $w>0$ is the smooth metric volume coefficient of [L2]; then $\delta_i\ge0$, it is a smooth density, and $\delta_i>0$ on $\{\rho_i>0\}$ whenever this set is nonempty. [L1, L2, construct]
items/lem-gr-finite-smooth-volume-density.md:92:2.1 (The masses are finite and the weights positive.) Fix $i$. Since $\operatorname{supp}\delta_i$ is compact, cover it by finitely many relatively compact coordinate balls and let $\{\theta_1,\dots,\theta_m\}$ be a subordinate finite smooth partition of unity. Applying the chart formula of [L5] with that finite cover exhibits $\mu_{\delta_i}(M)$ as a finite sum of Lebesgue integrals of bounded Borel functions supported in boxes; each term is finite by [L6], so $d_i:=\mu_{\delta_i}(M)<\infty$. Zero partition terms are allowed, so $d_i$ may be zero. Put $c_i:=(1+d_i)^{-1}\in(0,1]$. [step 1.1, L3, L4, L5, L6]
items/thm-qftx-scalar-eg-induction.md:123:[F5] [[lem-test-function-cutoffs-and-euclidean-localization]]: every open cover of an open Euclidean set has a locally finite smooth partition of unity subordinate to that cover.
items/thm-qftx-scalar-eg-induction.md:157:4.1 Apply [F5] to the open cover $\{C_I\}$ of $\mathbb M^n\setminus\Delta_n$, and use [A1] to assign each partition function to one cover member containing its support. The sum of the corresponding partition functions times $T^I_n$ is locally finite and defines a distribution $T_n^0$ on the complement of $\Delta_n$. Step 3.1 makes it independent of the partition choice locally; the cover is permutation-invariant, so a finite permutation average gives a symmetric extension on this complement. It satisfies causal factorization there by construction. [A1, F5, step 1.2, step 3.1, construct]
